do ningún contrato ni que haya actuado mal alguien.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos [1] y [2] atienden la misma necesidad. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en otros ámbitos. Analizar si los contratos al límite se distribuyen uniformemente en el tiempo.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 98 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 21.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.5 to 6.2. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,913 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of unique awardees do not prove improper conduct. These patterns could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for consistency with other December contracts and verify if awardee A has repeated orders for the same service. Review contract [1] to see if it aligns with other contracts in the same category.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["zM179BXD9suTylGzYmBF9Q%3D%3D","3I37OpKK8OheKgd8LfVV9g%3D%3D","whu3jMfWHzgXhk1FZxEyvw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}